**II** _intransitive_, **press hard,** [{{Refs 8th c.BC+|ἀμφ᾽ αὐτῷ πελεμίξαι ἐρείδοντες βελέεσσιν 8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 16.108; εἴς τινα Aristophanes Comicus [{5-6th c.BC}] “Nubes” 558; νέφος ἐ. ἐπὶ γῆν Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus [{1-2nd c.AD}] “Numa” 2; πνεῦμα κατὰ τῆς σχεδίας [prev\. author] “Crass.” 19}}]; of an illness or pain, **settle upon** a particular part, [{{Refs 5th c.BC+|νόσος ὁμότοιχος ἐ. Aeschylus Tragicus [{4-5th c.BC}] “Agamemnon” 1004 (Lyric poetry), compare 2nd c.AD: Rufus Medicus cited in 4th c.AD: Oribasius Medicus 45.30.27, 2nd c.AD: Galenus Medicus}}] 11.61; **exert pressure:** hence, **rest,** [{{Refs 2nd c.BC+|ἐπὶ τὸ ἔδαφος Hero Mechanicus [{2-1st c.BC} (?)] “Automatopoetica” 2.7}}].
**II.2** **set to work, fall to,** especially of eating, [{{Refs 6th c.BC+|ἔρειδε Aristophanes Comicus [{5-6th c.BC}] “Pax” 31, compare 25 (where, _accusative_ to Scholia, it is _metaphorically_ from rowers); ἐρείδετον [prev\. author] “fragment” 493}}].
**II.3** **become fixed,** {{Refs|πρῴρα ἐρείσασα “Act.Ap.” 27. 41.}}
