οῖς ἀγαθοῖς{{Refs 5th c.BC+|P 1. “P.” 4.285; πρὸς θεόν [prev. work]2.88; πρός τινα περί τινος 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Timoleon” 14; ὗς ποτ᾽ Ἀθαναίαν ἔριν ἤρισε 3rd c.BC: Theocritus Poeta Bucolicus 5.23; πρὸς πᾶν τὸ λεγόμενον 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 7.50}}; περί τινος about a thing, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 12.423, +others; περὶ μικρῶν ἀκριβῶς ἐ. 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 2.39}}: followed by a _relative_, ἐ. ὅστις ἀρείων {{Refs 5th c.BC+|3rd c.BC: Theocritus Poeta Bucolicus 5.67; ὁπότερος γενναιότερος 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Lysis” 207c}}: with _infinitive_, **contend** that.., ἤριζον οἱ πολλοὶ οὐ λυσιτελήσειν τὴν πάροδον {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 9.11}}: _absolutely_, of **sophistical disputations,** opposed to διαλέγεσθαι, ἀμφισβητεῖν, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Respublica” 454a, “Prt.” 337b, compare 4th c.BC: Crates Thebanus Poeta Philosophus 1.3}}; of political **discord,** with _dative_, Foed. cited in {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 5.79.}}
